    <http://example.org/node/chunk150> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must provide an intelligent assistance tool that supports clinical-administrative activities, including information retrieval, drafting medical and administrative documents, handling dossiers, and facilitating continuity of care." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk151> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, performance benchmarks, past AI use cases, and known trade-offs as of 2024, what is the proposed AI strategy for The solution, and how will our company's ensure high-quality outputs that meet the expected standards? the proposed AI strategy for this solution leverages our company's Retrieval-augmented generation capabilities to provide an intelligent assistance tool supporting clinical-administrative activities. our company's will employ our company's hybrid retrieval approach, combining lexical and semantic methods, to surface relevant information from the client's controlled corpus. employ will enable efficient information retrieval, drafting of medical and administrative documents, and handling of dossiers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk152> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure high-quality outputs, our company's will follow an iterative methodology, starting with corpus selection and curation in collaboration with the client's experts. our company's will then tune our company's retrieval model and design prompts and templates specific to each use case. our company's evaluation loop will assess answer quality using a labelled evaluation set built with the client, measuring groundedness, relevance, and factual support. our company's will also utilize our company's explainability features, including source citations, retrieved passages, and retrieval trace, to provide transparent and auditable outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk153> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Human oversight will be built into the workflow, with the assistant proposing and the professional validating, consistent with HAS guidance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk154> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of fine-tuning, our company's can optionally fine-tune our company's model on client material, subject to defined data use terms agreed upon with the client and our company's compliance function. our company's performance benchmarks indicate that our company's sovereign European open-weight model offers strong grounding behavior and explainability, although with somewhat lower raw performance on complex generative tasks. our company's past AI use cases, such as the medical-documentation pilot for a regional hospital group, demonstrate the effectiveness of our company's approach in reducing processing and documentation times while maintaining high-quality outputs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk155> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By applying these lessons learned and tailoring our company's solution to the client's specific needs, our company's can ensure that our company's intelligent assistance tool meets the expected standards and provides valuable support for clinical-administrative activities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

